  "data_abstract": "BNL-RHIC.  The paper includes measurements of the charged-particle jet yields at midrapidity by the STAR experiment in Au+Au collisions at 200 GeV. The jets were reconstructed with the anti-kT algorithm for resolution parameter R=0.2, 0.3, and 0.4 in central (0-10%) and peripheral (60-80%) centrality using a low cut on transverse momentum of jet constituents (pT>0.2 GeV/c). To suppress the large combinatorial background a cut on pT of a leading particle in jet is imposed.  From the charged-particle jet yields nuclear modification factor R_AA and R_CP are calculated along with the spectra ratios at various R.\n",
  "data_keywords": {
    "cmenergies": [
      {
        "gte": 200.0,
        "lte": 200.0
      }
    ],
    "observables": [
      "(1/Nevts)d2N/(2pi)(pTdpT)(deta)(dphi)",
      "RCP",
      "RAA",
      "R(pTlead",
      "R(0.2)/R(0.4)",
      "min=5)",
      "min=7/pTlead"
    ],
    "phrases": [
      "Inclusive",
      "Jet Production",
      "Differential Cross Section",
      "Heavy Ion Collisions"
    ],
    "reactions": [
      "Au Au --> X + jet"
    ]
  },
